<newsitem itemid="30643" id="root" date="1996-09-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>UK: Croda shows 22.5 million stg profit in H1.</title>
<headline>Croda shows 22.5 million stg profit in H1.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		11.5		   vs 10.9</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	 3.45		   vs 3.25</p>
<p> Pretax profit	    22.5		   vs 21.5</p>
<p> Turnover		   229.6		  vs 221.1</p>
<p> Operating result	 24.8		   vs 23.8</p>
<p> Interest paid	    2.3		    vs 2.3</p>
<p> Net taxed		  15.6		   vs 14.7</p>
<p> Attributable	     15.5		   vs 14.5</p>
<p> Pay date		   December 2, 1996</p>
<p>Div registration date  September 17, 1996</p>
<p>NOTE - Speciality chemicals group Croda International Plc said chemicals, which accounted for 80 percent of turnover, had performed well. &quot;The trading outlook...is healthy. Whilst European demand was subdued in the first half, there are clear signs of a nascent recovery and there is steady economic growth in many of the other parts of the world. Unless there is an unforeseen change in trading conditions, we believe the year's results should be good,&quot; said chairman Michael Valentine.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
